{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The Sidonians call Hermon Sirion, and the Amorites call it Senir.</b> See here three names, and it is written (Deuteronomy 4:48) ״ועד הר שיאון הוא חרמון״ — see here that it was called by four names: Hermon, Sirion, Senir, Siyon. And why did they need to write them? To tell the praise of the land of Israel, that each and every one of the kings of the nations would call his place by the name of the land of Israel — as much as to say that four kingdoms glory in it: this one says, 'it is called after my name,' and that one says, 'it is called after my name.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:59.093240164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}